## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Create React App project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package:**
- Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to project dependencies
- Used `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts with Create React App

**2. Modified Files:**
- `package.json`: Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
- `package-lock.json`: Updated with new package and dependency tree
- `src/App.js`: 
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the App component (after Footer, inside the Router)

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the React-specific integration:

1. **Framework Identified:** Create React App (react-scripts 5.0.1)
2. **Package Manager:** npm
3. **Integration Point:** Main App component (`src/App.js`)

The Analytics component was placed at the end of the main App div, which ensures it tracks all route changes since it's inside the Router component.

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully without errors
- ✅ Package installed and added to dependencies
- ✅ Code follows existing project patterns and structure
- ✅ Analytics component correctly imported and integrated

### Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section for your project
3. After deployment and user visits, analytics data will appear in the dashboard

### Notes

- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals
- It works seamlessly with React Router for SPA navigation tracking
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- Analytics data will only be collected when deployed to Vercel's platform
